{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5obj544s6sbwoskkb2lddngdoqzhzg47p7rt5xzwolqskb2rc2ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `Bash` and `Read` are unresponsive, so I can't do the final on-disk check. Here's my write-up, separating what I directly observed from what I couldn't.\n\n## ⚠️ Do this first: check `src/lib.rs` is pristine\n\nMy last action was re-running `mutation_check.sh`, which **deliberately mutates `translation/src/lib.rs`** and restores it via a `trap ... EXIT`. That run produced **no output** and the tool died immediately after. I could not confirm the restore fired.\n\n```\ndiff /tmp/claude/lib.rs.safety translation/src/lib.rs   # I made this backup before the first run\n# or: git -C translation diff src/lib.rs\n```\nIf they differ, restore from `/tmp/claude/lib.rs.safety`. The first mutation run *did* print `src/lib.rs restored and building`, so that backup is the pristine original.\n\nAlso treat `mutation_check.sh` itself as suspect: my last 5 edits to it returned empty/garbled responses, so it may be half-edited.\n\n## What I verified with my own eyes\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | clean, no errors |\n| C `.so` build (cmake) | `libharvest-work-nTzw79.so` |\n| `nm -D` C exports | **exactly one**: `jumpnode` |\n| `nm -D` Rust exports (default) | **exactly one**: `jumpnode` → 0 missing, 0 extra |\n| `nm -D` Rust exports (feature) | `jumpnode` + `jumpnode_initialize_test_data` → 0 missing |\n| `check_all_features.sh` | **ALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS VERIFIED** — 25 tests default, 47 with feature |\n| `--release` soak (`soak.rs`) | 6 passed |\n| `--release` tree soak | 18 passed |\n| Mutation run #1 | 17 of 22 mutants caught |\n\nArtifacts created: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (12 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (25 rows), 7 test files, `tests/csupport/init_shim.c`, 2 scripts. `libloading = \"0.8\"` added to dev-dependencies. **`c_src/` was never modified.**\n\n## The finding that shapes everything\n\n`initialize_test_data()` is `static` and **never called**. So in the shipped `.so`, `node_count == 0` forever, `find_node_by_id()` *always* returns NULL, and modes 1/2/4 *always* early-return. The entire observable behavior is:\n\n- mode 1 → `18`, mode 2 → `34`, mode 4 → `66`, anything else → `130`\n- mode 3 → `2*strlen(\"Node_%d_Depth_%d\") + 8 + (flags & 0177)` ← the only arm that computes\n\nThe Rust reproduces this exactly. To actually test the dead-but-translated code, I compiled a shim **outside** `c_src` that `#include`s the pristine `lib.c` and exports a wrapper for `initialize_test_data`, mirroring Rust's `expose_init_test_data` feature — so modes 1/2/4, `add_node`, `process_backward` and `safe_double_to_int` were compared against real C, not assumptions.\n\n**No divergence was found on any defined input.**\n\n## Three substantive discoveries\n\n**1. The C `.so` has an unresolved `sqrt`.** `CMakeLists.txt` never links libm. An `RTLD_NOW` dlopen of the C library fails outright with `undefined symbol: sqrt`. It only works in practice because `RTLD_LAZY` defers the binding and case `0004` always early-returns before reaching `sqrt`. The Rust `.so` needs no libm at all (inline `sqrtsd`). This is a latent fragility in the C packaging, not a translation defect — but it made one of my tests flaky until I scoped the `RTLD_NOW` assertion to the Rust side only.\n\n**2. Mode 2 with negative `depth` is the one place a caller can observe a difference.** `process_backward` reads before `temp_array`; C reads stack garbage, Rust reads its zero-initialized array. Measured: all 6 probes differed (depth=-1 → C=`23480`, Rust=`1694`). This is genuine UB in the C and **cannot** be matched deterministically — I documented it (ERRORS.md row 10) and deliberately did not assert equality. Flagging it as a conscious decision you may want to revisit.\n\n**3. Two \"failures\" were my errors, not the Rust's.** At `depth=i32::MAX` mode 4 saturates to `2147483647`, then `result += 82` overflows and wraps to `-2147483567` — both libraries identically. And my saturation-boundary depths (2e7) were ~8× too small: `acc0 ≈ 133.658`, so the clamp only engages past ~1.64e8. I fixed the tests, never the Rust.\n\n## Mutation testing: the 5 survivors are mostly *equivalent mutants*\n\nThis was the most useful step. I verified with a separate exhaustive search that 4 of the 5 survivors are genuinely unobservable through the public API, not test gaps:\n\n- `parent_id != -1` → `!= -2` — **equivalent**: no node has id `-1`, so `find_node_by_id` returns NULL and the `break` gives an identical result. The C's root sentinel is redundant.\n- `40.0625` → `40.0626` — unobservable; exhaustive search over (node_id 1..7 × depth 0..9) found no distinguishing input, because everything is integer-truncated.\n- both `safe_double_to_int` threshold mutants — equivalent, because Rust's `as i32` saturates in exactly that gap, *and* no integer depth lands the product in the 1-wide sensitive window (step is ~13.37 per depth unit).\n- `intstr_zero_case` — my sed emitted `n += 0`, a literal no-op. Bad mutant, my mistake.\n\nA corollary worth knowing: mode 3 depends **only on `strlen`**, so digit *values* are unobservable — only decimal *widths* matter. I covered widths 1..11 exhaustively for both fields.\n\n## What I could NOT verify — the gate is NOT closed\n\n1. **`src/lib.rs` pristine state** — critical, see top.\n2. **`mutation_check.sh` final state** — my last 5 edits are unconfirmed; the re-run with observable replacement mutants never produced output.\n3. **Consolidated re-run after the soak additions.** `check_all_features.sh` passed *before* I added `soak.rs` and the 4 tree-soak tests. Those new tests each passed standalone in `--release`, but the all-combinations script wasn't re-run afterward. Expect ~31 default / ~57 feature tests.\n\nTo close it out once your shell is back:\n```\ncd translation && bash check_all_features.sh && bash mutation_check.sh\n```\nPhases A–C are substantively complete and passing; Phase D's symbol diff reached empty in both combos. What remains is re-confirmation, not new work — but I'd not call verification done until that final consolidated run is green and `src/lib.rs` is confirmed unmutated."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4485,"cache_read_input_tokens":120745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4485,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8aa1068f-07f1-4d4f-8336-7fd5e05f263c","uuid":"87831ab0-34e4-46b7-9361-a42c4444bbe3","timestamp":"2026-08-28T02:48:18.902Z"}
